WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.670
February might be the shortest month of the
year, but Netflix still has a long list of

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.100
new offerings coming your way.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.520
Whether you're craving amazing action or dizzying
drama, there's something for everyone.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.540
From horror to hilarity, it's all here for
your viewing pleasure in February.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:16.820
Looking for some action?

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.320
You've come to the right place.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.280
Beginning February 1st, you can check out
Dirty Harry, the 1971 film that first introduced

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.420
us to Clint Eastwood's iconic detective.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.680
You know the one.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.880
"You could ask yourself a question: Do I feel
lucky?"

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.260
The 1967 classic The Dirty Dozen is also coming
to Netflix on February 1st.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:43.880
It tells the tale of twelve Death Row convicts
who improbably become soliders, infiltrating

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.960
a Nazi powwow just before D-Day.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:46.980
Go team!

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.400
If you're looking for altogether lighter fare,
there's always The Other Guys, a buddy-cop

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.600
film starring Will Ferrell and Mark Wahlberg.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.460
When a minor case unearths a much more serious
crime, two down-on-their-luck cops realize

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.420
they have the perfect chance to prove their
mettle.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.140
Here's a tantalizing taste of what these down-to-earth
crimefighters can do.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.760
"Who's got the golden goose now, huh?"

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.840
The Other Guys starts streaming on February
1st.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.300
Craving sci-fi served with a side of satire?

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.580
Starship Troopers will surely hit the spot.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:25.470
Directed by inscrutable Dutch provocateur
Paul Verhoeven, the film involves an all-out

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.280
war between Earth and a bunch of extraterrestrial
bugs.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.620
But it also serves as a fantastic military
satire.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.280
This underrated gem really piles on the gore
and hammy acting.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:37.960
Did we mention the alien insects?

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.380
[Aliens screeching.]

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.840
Starship Troopers hurdles your way on February
15th.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.960
Fans of Blade Runner will definitely want
to check out Ridley Scott's Final Cut.

00:01:50.969 --> 00:01:55.380
Yes, it's just one of many versions of the
film - but this is the only one where Scott

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.000
had complete creative control over every frame.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.220
The sci-fi opus starts streaming on February
1st.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:04.959
If you've never seen it before, here's your
chance - so run, don't walk.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:10.099
There's so much gut-wrenching drama coming
to Netflix in February, so go ahead and consider

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.680
your world effectively shattered.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.760
First up: Roman Polanski's The Pianist, starring
Adrien Brody.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.719
Based on a true story, it involves a classical
musician who manages to survive the Holocaust

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.240
against incredible odds.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.680
The film - which won three Academy Awards
- hits the streamer on February 1st.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.440
Then there's Driving Miss Daisy, the 1989
drama starring Morgan Freeman and Jessica

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:31.940
Tandy.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.960
It depicts the burgeoning friendship between
a headstrong widow and her supernaturally

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.040
patient chauffeur.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:42.240
The film won four Oscars, including Best Picture,
and it's coming your way on February 1st.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.000
Last but not least, Prince's semi-autobiographical
musical drama Purple Rain also starts streaming

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.020
on February 1st.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.460
It tells the story of a fiery young musician
whose band is about to make it big.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:58.120
The film deservedly took home an Academy Award
for the score, which features "Let's Go Crazy,"

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.420
"When Doves Cry," and the epic title track.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.500
Here's an icebreaker for you: Do you like
the Police Academy movies?

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.140
If so, February is officially your month.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.480
Seven installments of the comedy series are
coming to the streamer on February 1st.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.740
And while you're at it, why not throw Scary
Movie 2 and A Haunted House into the mix?

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:20.300
They start streaming on February 1st and February
21st, respectively.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.840
Here's a little teaser for you:

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.040
"What happened to your furniture, 'cuz?"

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.080
Sex and the City 2 also starts streaming February
1st, and it goes a little something like this:

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:33.120
"What do you think?"

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.240
"This is fabulous!" *phone rings* "There's
my phone!

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.780
Oh my god, here's my phone!"

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.780
"Who's her long distance provider?"

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.360
Want to see something really scary?

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.489
Take a good long stare at Polaroid, which
tells the story of a high school outcast who

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:49.359
discovers an old camera — but there's a
catch.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.740
Anyone photographed by the camera comes to
a very grisly end.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.940
Say cheese!

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.320
You can start streaming - and screaming - on
February 9th.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:02.180
Then there's Girl on the Third Floor, the
story of a man who just wants to remodel his

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.440
new home and live happily ever after with
his blossoming family.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:09.340
Unfortunately, this house was born bad - and
it's out for blood.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.580
Check it out beginning February 22nd.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:17.139
Finally, there's Every Time I Die, which has
quite the mind-melting plot: After a man meets

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:21.590
an early death, his consciousness keeps zipping
into the bodies of his close friends.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:25.150
Turns out, he's hoping to protect them from
the same person who killed him.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.080
Will he succeed?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.280
Find out for yourself when the movie starts
streaming on February 25th.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.460
As for TV offerings, we're super-excited for
the first season of Locke &amp; Key, based on

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.580
the critically-acclaimed comic book series
written by Joe Hill.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.360
Expect lots of near-indescribable weirdness
- our favorite kind.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.520
You can give it a whirl on February 7th.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.751
On the comedy side, there's only one new stand-up
set coming to Netflix in February 2020, but

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.500
it should be quite the doozy.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.340
On February 4th, veteran comic Tom Papa drops
his fifth set of all-new material, You're

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:56.120
Doing Great!

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.980
For the uninitiated, here's Papa talking about
his daughter:

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.240
"We have a Mean Girl.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.280
Yeah, I didn't know they were real.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.280
I feel guilty.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.660
I made it, I feed it, I'm keeping it alive."

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.040
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:12.520
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies and TV shows are coming soon.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:16.280
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

